# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-call proof memo
#
# The window-proof bundle capabilities normalize and recompute the same deep
# credential many times within one top-level call: a window proof appears as
# a bundle member, as a non-null change side, and inside adjacent diffs, and
# every layer re-normalizes everything below it. The memo gives each
# top-level call one shared cache so every unique equal-valued deep proof is
# normalized and recomputed at most once per call, and so canonical key
# order, member digests, stage chains, and diff digests reuse the
# intermediate values already computed for equal content.
#
# Cache identity is a type-exact structural key (dict key order is
# insignificant; lists stay distinct from tuples, bools from ints), never
# object identity: the ``id`` shortcut only avoids re-walking the *same*
# object within one call, and the strong reference held alongside keeps that
# id valid while the memo lives, so different values never merge. The memo
# is dropped when the top-level call returns, so mutating an input between
# calls cannot observe stale entries. Cached results are treated as
# immutable everywhere; every public result is still assembled from fresh
# deep copies, so no two returned levels share a mutable container.


